course: dictionary
lesson: 6590
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and nobility is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: As a noun for people, the nobility means the people of the highest social class, such as dukes, earls and lords, whose titles pass down in their families. «In 1648 Hetman Bohdan Khmelnytsky led a huge uprising against the Polish-Lithuanian nobility.» The word against is the clue: you rise up against a group of powerful people, so here nobility means that group.
explain: As a quality, nobility means being good, honest and brave. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about a group of people, or about how someone behaves? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The nobility means the people of the highest social class, such as dukes, earls and lords.
fact: Titles of the nobility are passed down in families.
fact: Nobility also means the quality of being noble: good, honest and brave.
fact: «Uprising» means a sudden fight against those in power.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «In 1648 Hetman Bohdan Khmelnytsky led a huge uprising against the Polish-Lithuanian nobility.» What does the nobility mean here? | Farmers who work the land | The quality of being brave and honest | *The people of the highest social class, such as dukes and lords | A type of castle
exercise: Maya says her grandad showed nobility when he returned the lost purse. What does nobility mean here? | *The quality of being good, honest and brave | A loud argument | A title passed down in a family | The people of the highest social class
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to nobility when it means being good, honest and brave? | Uprising | Castles | Titles | *Honour
test: Dukes, earls and lords all belong to which group? | *The nobility | The Hetmanate | The uprising | The Cossacks
test: Jayden reads, «She showed great nobility when she forgave her brother.» What does nobility mean? | *Being good, honest and brave | Belonging to a family with a title | Fighting in a war | Living in a castle
exam: Read: «In 1648 Hetman Bohdan Khmelnytsky led a huge uprising against the Polish-Lithuanian nobility.» Which clue shows that nobility means a group of people? | The word huge, which is about size | *The word against, because you rise up against people | The word 1648, which is a date | The word led, which is about a leader
